      "worked": "Partition $[0,1]$ into ten disjoint intervals:\n$$[0,0.1),\\ [0.1,0.2),\\ \\ldots,\\ [0.8,0.9),\\ [0.9,1].$$\nAssign each of the eleven points to its interval. By the pigeonhole principle, at least one of the ten intervals contains two points. Each interval has length $0.1$, so the distance between these two points is at most $0.1$ units.",
